            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I am not sure why documented approach wouldn't work.\r\n\r\nDoes next setting behave not the same as this one?\r\n```lua\r\ninput = { \"%b[]\", \"^%[[^%s%[%]]*%s*().*()%]$\" },\r\n```\r\n",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I am not sure why documented approach wouldn't work.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Does next setting behave not the same as this one?</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"input = { &quot;%b[]&quot;, &quot;^%[[^%s%[%]]*%s*().*()%]$&quot; },\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">input</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>%b[]<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>^%[[^%s%[%]]*%s*().*()%]$<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>},</pre></div>",
            "bodyText": "I am not sure why documented approach wouldn't work.\nDoes next setting behave not the same as this one?\ninput = { \"%b[]\", \"^%[[^%s%[%]]*%s*().*()%]$\" },",
