                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "Oh, probably because one example shows those patterns merged together. It doesn't *need* to be, it was just an example.\r\n\r\nTransition should literally just be:\r\n- Remove `find = ` and `extract = `.\r\n- Move `(` of left match to its right part (forming `()`).\r\n- Move `)` of right match to its left part (also forming `()`).",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Oh, probably because one example shows those patterns merged together. It doesn't <em>need</em> to be, it was just an example.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Transition should literally just be:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Remove <code class=\"notranslate\">find = </code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">extract = </code>.</li>\n<li>Move <code class=\"notranslate\">(</code> of left match to its right part (forming <code class=\"notranslate\">()</code>).</li>\n<li>Move <code class=\"notranslate\">)</code> of right match to its left part (also forming <code class=\"notranslate\">()</code>).</li>\n</ul>",
                    "bodyText": "Oh, probably because one example shows those patterns merged together. It doesn't need to be, it was just an example.\nTransition should literally just be:\n\nRemove find =  and extract = .\nMove ( of left match to its right part (forming ()).\nMove ) of right match to its left part (also forming ()).",
